package archrules

// WriteDisciplineAllowed is the write-discipline gate's shrinking allowlist:
// a durable "file.go#Symbol" reference mapped to the fix required to remove
// the entry. It is generated MECHANICALLY — run the gate with an empty map
// and transcribe what it reports — so the baseline records exactly what the
// scan sees, and it only ever tightens: a raw filesystem write is migrated
// to safefs and its entry deleted, never added without a reason. The analyzer
// fails an entry the scan no longer reports. Directory and removal ops
// (os.Mkdir/MkdirAll/Remove/RemoveAll/Chmod) are writes to the gate too; the
// entries tagged "fsgate baseline" are the sites it found when they joined.
